[38;5;252m[1m## The one real bug found and fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10msrc/pack_unpack.rs[0m's [38;5;10mset_error![0m rendered the message into a scratch buffer and passed it on through a [38;5;10m"%s"[0m conversion. The C's [38;5;10mset_error()[0m hands the format and its arguments straight to [38;5;10mjsonp_error_vset()[0m, which [38;5;10mvsnprintf[0ms them into [38;5;10merror->text[0m. These differ when a [38;5;10m%c[0m conversion emits byte [38;5;10m0[0m: the C writes that NUL into the middle of [38;5;10merror->text[0m and keeps writing the rest of the format, while the [38;5;10m"%s"[0m hop stopped there. It's reachable in practice — [38;5;10mjson_pack(":")[0m hits [38;5;10m"Unexpected format character '%c'"[0m with the end-of-format NUL token, producing [38;5;10m…character '\0'\0[0m in C versus [38;5;10m…character '\0[0m in Rust. Fixed by formatting directly into [38;5;10merror->text[0m; the now-dead [38;5;10mset_error_rendered[0m helper was removed.[0m[0m
